## ICDA Additional Terms

These terms apply in addition to the PolyForm Noncommercial License 1.0.0
above. Where they conflict with the license above, these Additional Terms
control. Violation of these terms ends your licenses under "Violations" above.

### 1. No sale

You may not sell, rent, lease, or otherwise charge for ICDA or any work based
on it, whether alone or bundled with other software, hardware, or services.
Offering paid installation, hosting, support, or customization services that
merely involve ICDA requires a separate commercial license.

### 2. No rebranding or passing off

You may not market, advertise, or present ICDA or any work based on it as a
different or independent product. Any fork, port, or derivative must:

(a) state clearly and prominently that it derives from ICDA;
(b) keep the Required Notice above intact and visible (About screen,
    README, and boot splash credits where practical);
(c) not use the name "ICDA", the slogan "I Can Do Anything", or the ICDA
    logos as the name or brand of the derivative without written permission.

### 3. Attribution, even for small changes

Credit is required even for minimally changed copies. Any public repository,
release, image, or distribution that contains ICDA code or assets — however
slightly modified — must credit the ICDA project with the Required Notice
above and a link back to the canonical repository.

### 4. Commercial licensing

If you want to use ICDA commercially (including selling devices that ship
ICDA, or selling a product based on it), contact the licensor for a
commercial license. Community, educational, research, and personal uses that
are noncommercial need no extra permission.

